# CompTIA A+ — Mobile & Cloud

Which cloud model delivers ready-to-use applications over the internet?
---
SaaS
~ IaaS
~ PaaS
~ DaaS
---
Software as a Service, like Gmail or Office 365. You manage nothing but your data.

Which cloud model rents raw virtual machines, storage, and networks?
---
IaaS
~ SaaS
~ PaaS
~ FaaS
---
Infrastructure as a Service, like EC2. You manage the OS and everything above it.

Which cloud model gives developers a managed platform to deploy code without handling servers?
---
PaaS
~ IaaS
~ SaaS
~ DaaS
---
Platform as a Service, like Heroku or App Engine.

A cloud used exclusively by one organization is called what?
---
Private cloud
~ Public cloud
~ Hybrid cloud
~ Community cloud
---
Hybrid mixes private and public. Community is shared by organizations with common needs.

What does a hypervisor do?
---
Runs virtual machines on physical hardware
~ Encrypts virtual disks
~ Balances load between servers
~ Manages container images
---
Type 1 runs on bare metal, like ESXi or Hyper-V. Type 2 runs on a host OS, like VirtualBox.

Which CPU feature must be enabled in firmware before VMs will run well?
---
Virtualization support
~ Secure Boot
~ XMP
~ Hyper-Threading
---
Intel VT-x or AMD-V, toggled in the UEFI setup.

Which mobile display technology lights each pixel individually, giving true blacks?
---
OLED
~ IPS LCD
~ TN LCD
~ Mini-LED
---
No backlight. A black pixel is simply off, which also saves battery in dark mode.

Which technology lets a phone make payments by holding it near a terminal?
---
NFC
~ Bluetooth
~ Wi-Fi Direct
~ Infrared
---
Near Field Communication, a few centimetres of range by design.

What does enabling airplane mode do?
---
Disables all wireless radios at once
~ Powers the phone off
~ Locks the SIM card
~ Disables mobile data only
---
Cellular, Wi-Fi, and Bluetooth all drop, though Wi-Fi can be re-enabled on top of it.

Which sync method lets corporate email enforce a passcode on an employee's phone?
---
MDM policies
~ POP3
~ NFC
~ Location services
---
Mobile Device Management can require encryption, remote-wipe lost devices, and separate work data.

A phone's touchscreen responds in the wrong places. What is the common name for this?
---
Ghost touch
~ Burn-in
~ Dead pixel
~ Latency
---
Digitizer faults, a failing screen protector, or moisture. Calibration or screen replacement fixes it.

What is the risk of installing apps from outside the official app store?
---
Malware from untrusted sources
~ Higher battery drain
~ Slower updates only
~ Voided cellular contract
---
Sideloading skips the store's vetting. On the exam it is the classic cause of a compromised phone.
